// Prism golden set v2.
//
// WHY THIS SIZE. The eval harness reports paired bootstrap intervals, and the
// smallest effect an interval can resolve is set by the number of examples:
//
//     test examples      9     25     50    100    200    400
//     smallest gain   none  16.0%   8.0%   4.0%   2.0%   1.0%
//     detectable
//
// v1 had 9 test examples, which detects nothing at all -- the harness was
// correct and the dataset made it useless. This file has ~200 across splits so
// the gate can resolve a ~3% change, which is roughly the size of a real prompt
// improvement.
//
// SPLITS ARE A CONTAMINATION BOUNDARY. router_train exists so the week-9 router
// never trains on what it is scored against; calibration holds the open-ended
// comparisons a human labels for judge kappa. load() rejects ids that repeat
// across splits.
//
// SCORING LIVES IN THE DATA. An example with references is scored
// programmatically; one without goes to the judge. Keeping that here stops a run
// from quietly promoting hard examples to the judge (generous) or demoting
// open-ended ones to exact match (brutal).

// ===================== test: factual QA, exact match ======================
